file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh exports STANDING_CARD_LIVE naming the pen record it already keeps, with the tree-write trap named
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scan.sh builds the effective record in two awk passes, reports runs_live, and its header paragraph now describes a repair rather than a disclosed limit
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_control.sh 21 new readings both directions plus the end-to-end runner case, and run_scan clears the inherited variable
file tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish 23 new legs, and the header molted C+/77 to B/84 under a cairn
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the roster comment carries the repair, the declined shapes, and the measured 182-in-13s
file construction/REDS.md %483 closed and folded to its shelf; %488 booked; the census 487 to 488
file construction/archive/REDS-the-guard-that-read-the-last-pass-rows-483.md the shelf, with the row whole
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md the witness-header molt cairn
file construction/ITINERARY.md the round's block, cut to 721 bytes out of my own prose, and the git nib
recommend check-in (Claude) -- %488 is the next lap in this lane and it wants a ruling before code: a pre-push hook is the first thing in this tree that would refuse a PUSH rather than a commit, and refusing a push is a different weight from refusing a commit -- a hand mid-send with a refused push has fewer moves than one with a refused commit. The instrument is cheap (conflict_marker measures 0.3s whole-tree) and the pen is ordinary; what wants a word is whether the fleet wants a gate there at all, or only an announcement. Everything else in this lane is kg.
